From 16410e4ff3cb6db229bf351b18479fa067fb07ca Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 9 Sep 2026 13:40:43 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix: make Reputation Manager crons respect each client's own
 timezone
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

All 6 rep-* crons (engine-panel, trustpilot-watch, reddit-watch,
twitter-watch, crisis-response, digest) were fixed-UTC Inngest triggers —
an operator's per-engagement "Client timezone" setting had zero effect
on any of them, unlike Showtime's nightly-briefs/credential-health/
lost-deal-sweep/weekly-metrics, which already resolve to each
engagement's own local hour via matchesDailyLocalHour.

Converted all 6 to the same hourly-dispatch + matchesDailyLocalHour
pattern, staggered across distinct local hours (7/8/9/10/11/18) so the
existing watch-before-crisis-response-before-digest ordering holds
per-client regardless of that client's timezone.

Also: the Reputation Manager "new client" route never seeded
stack.timezone at all (defaulting silently to UTC forever unless someone
happened to open Edit stack settings) — now seeded from the workspace's
own Settings > Timezones & Region default, same as Showtime's engagement
wizard already does. Updated the Client-timezone field's help text, which
previously named only the 4 Showtime crons it affected.

Verified: tsc --noEmit clean, next build succeeds, eslint shows no new
errors on touched files (the 2 flagged in edit-stack-settings.tsx predate
this change, confirmed against the prior commit).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
